$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 8-(3-Chloro-5-(4-(4-methylpiperazin-1-
yl)phenyl)pyridin-4-yl)-2,8-diazaspiro[4.5]decan-1-one (68). 8-(3-
Bromo-5-chloropyridin-4-yl)-2,8-diazaspiro[4.5]decan-1-one (57) (35 mg,
0.10 mmol),
1-methyl-4-(4-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)phenyl)piperazine
(34 mg, 0.11 mmol), and Pd(dppf)Cl2· CH2Cl2 (3.7 mg, 5.1 μmol) were
loaded in a microwave vial under argon, and then degassed MeCN (1.8 mL)
and 0.5 M aqueous sodium carbonate solution (284 μL, 0.142 mmol) were
added. The reaction mixture was heated under microwave irradiation at 120
°C for 60 min. The solvent was evaporated and the crude material was
dry-loaded and purified via Biotage column chromatography (CH2Cl2/MeOH
97/3 to 85/15). The title compound 68 (38 mg, 85% yield) as a cream
solid. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.32−1.38 (m, 2H), 1.94−2.02 (m, 4H),
2.39 (s, 3H), 2.60−2.65 (m, 4H), 2.70−2.78 (m, 2H), 3.11− 3.17 (m, 2H),
3.27−3.31 (m, 6H), 5.54 (br s, 1H), 7.00 (d, J = 8.7 Hz, 2H), 7.19 (d, J
= 8.7 Hz, 2H), 8.18 (s, 1H), 8.39 (s, 1H); 13C NMR (126 MHz, CDCl3) δ
31.4, 32.4, 38.8, 42.0, 46.1, 47.7, 48.6, 55.0, 115.7, 128.3, 128.7,
130.1, 133.9, 149.1, 150.6, 151.0, 152.9, 181.8; LC−MS (method C, ESI,
m/z) t R = 1.43 min, 440/442 (M + H)+; ESI-HRMS calcd for C24H31 35ClN5O
(M + H)+ 440.2212, found 440.2205.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, microwave irradiation, thermal, microwave vial used,
Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of Potent, Orally Bioavailable, Small-Molecule Inhibitors of
WNT Signaling from a Cell-Based Pathway Screen
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Mallinger, Aurelie; Crumpler, Simon; Pichowicz, Mark; Waalboer, Dennis;
