$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM N-(6-(6-Ethyl-5-methoxypyridin-3-yl)benzo[d]thiazol-2-yl)acetamide 11 1 A
mixture of
N-(6-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)benzo[d]thiazol-2-yl)acetamide
27 (100 mg, 0.314 mmol), 5-bromo-2-ethyl-3-methoxypyridine (95 mg, 0.44
mmol) and cesium carbonate (1.33M, 0.943 mmol) was stirred in a sealed
tube. PdCl2(dppf).CH2Cl2 (25.7 mg, 0.0314 mmol) was added and the mixture
stirred at 110 ºC for 1 h. The reaction was diluted with EtOAc and washed
with water. The aqueous layer was further extracted with EtOAc and the
combined organic layers washed with water, brine, dried (Na2SO4),
filtered through a pad of florisil and the clear solution concentrated.
Trituration with MeOH.
N-(6-(6-ethyl-5-methoxypyridin-3-yl)benzo[d]thiazol-2-yl)acetamide 11
(75.9 mg, 74%) as a white solid. 1H NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d 6) δ 12.38 (s,
1H), 8.41-8.37 (m, 2H), 7.83-7.78 (m, 2H), 7.62 (d, J = 1.7 Hz, 1H), 3.94
(s, 3H), 2.78 (q, J = 7.5 Hz, 2H), 2.22 (s, 3H), 1.21 (t, J = 7.5 Hz,
3H); ESMS (M+H) 328.15.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling, sealed tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Structural Basis for Isoform Selectivity in a Class of Benzothiazole
Inhibitors of Phosphoinositide 3-Kinase γ
